        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nI need the full history of changes and projections off it. Key-value entity or event sourced?",
          "label": "evals/akka-sdk-key-value-entities/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "3e304803a50c8734927e8af6990274b49b4247cea2e2e209cea68d65819ead49",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "**Event sourced entity.** Key-value entities store only the latest state, so the history is gone. An event sourced entity persists every change as an event, so you have the full history by construction.\n\nProjections come from a View with `@Consume.FromEventSourcedEntity`, which builds the read model from the event stream. You can also use a Consumer to push events to a topic or another service.\n\nChoose key-value instead only if you need current state and nothing else. You can't add history to a key-value entity later without migrating."
        },
